-- title:
--   Theorem 2.1 — determinacy for reachability, discounted-sum and limit-average objectives
-- statement:
--   For every concurrent stochastic game, every state $s$, and every objective $\varphi$ that is a reachability objective $\mathrm{Reach}(T)$, a discounted-sum objective $\mathrm{Disc}(r,\lambda)$ (reward $r$ with values in $[0,1]$, $\lambda\in[0,1)$), or a limit-average objective $\mathrm{LimAvg}(r)$ (reward with values in $[0,1]$),
--   $$\sup_{\sigma\in\Sigma}\inf_{\tau\in\Gamma}\mathbb E^{\sigma,\tau}_s[\varphi]=\inf_{\tau\in\Gamma}\sup_{\sigma\in\Sigma}\mathbb E^{\sigma,\tau}_s[\varphi],$$
--   where $\Sigma,\Gamma$ are all (history-dependent, randomized) strategies.
--
--   Determinacy makes the value $\mathrm{val}_\varphi$ well defined independently of the order of quantification, which every other statement uses.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a finite game G = (S, A, B, δ) with |S| = n and at most m actions per player → states Fin n, actions Fin mA and Fin mB with n, mA, mB ≥ 1, m = max(mA, mB), distributions as nonnegative real vectors summing to one; reason: relabelling of finite sets; nonempty state and action sets are the source game convention
--   - encoding: the probability measure on valid plays Ω_s generated by finite histories, strategies on valid histories → the Ionescu-Tulcea trajectory measure on all sequences in (S × A × B)^ℕ; strategies are defined on all finite stage lists; reason: invalid plays have probability zero and values of strategies on invalid histories never matter, so every expectation and value is unchanged
-- source:
--   Ali Asadi, Krishnendu Chatterjee, The Computational Complexity of Concurrent Stochastic Games: Exact Value and Approximation, STOC 2027 submission #285 (October 2026), SHA-256 5cff187cf6b230b3bdfe540f2832f824d1ddb6acb43239fbf469d37c43b0d461, https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/285.pdf, Theorem 2.1 ([Eve57, Sha53, MN81]), printed p. 4 (PDF p. 6)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ConcurrentStochasticApprox_Approx_Game
open Finset

namespace ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx

/-- **Theorem 2.1 (Determinacy).** For every concurrent stochastic game, every state `s`, and every
reachability, discounted-sum or limit-average objective `φ`,
`sup_σ inf_τ E_s^{σ,τ}[φ] = inf_τ sup_σ E_s^{σ,τ}[φ]`. -/
theorem theorem_2_1 {n mA mB : ℕ} (G : CSG n mA mB) (s : Fin n) :
    (∀ T : Finset (Fin n), value G (reachObj T) s = upperValue G (reachObj T) s) ∧
    (∀ r : Reward n mA mB, IsReward r → ∀ lam : ℝ, 0 ≤ lam → lam < 1 →
      value G (discObj r lam) s = upperValue G (discObj r lam) s) ∧
    (∀ r : Reward n mA mB, IsReward r →
      value G (limAvgObj r) s = upperValue G (limAvgObj r) s) := by sorry

end ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx
